w: That man hath per- fect bless- ed- ness who walk- eth not a- stray
w: Nor sit- teth in the scorn- er's chair: But plac- eth his de- light
w: He shall be like a tree that grows Near plant- ed by a riv'r,
w: And all he doth shall pros- per well. The wick- ed are not so;
w: In judg- ment there- fore shall not stand Such as un- god- ly are;
w: For why? the way of god- ly men Un- to the Lord is known:
A | A B c A | F G A A | G F F E | F3 |]
w: In coun- sel of un- god- ly men, nor stands in sin- ners' way,
w: U- pon God's law, and med- i- tates On his law day and night.
w: Which in his sea- son yields his fruit, And his leaf fad- eth nev'r:
w: But like they are un- to the chaff, Which wind drives to and fro.
w: Nor in th'as- sem- bly of the just Shall wick- ed men ap- pear.
w: Where- as the way of wick- ed men Shall quite be o- ver- thrown.
